  "step1_summary": "- Chief complaint: low mood, low appetite, low energy/fatigue; intermittent shortness of breath and palpitations; nausea; unintentional weight loss.\n- Onset/duration/severity/aggravating-alleviating factors:\n  - Low mood and low energy: months in duration; patient reports feeling \"down\" for a long time and changed when he moved to a new law firm (~3–6 months timeline).\n  - Loss of appetite began ~3.5 months ago after job change; weight loss ~1 stone (~6–7 kg) over ~6 months.\n  - Shortness of breath and palpitations: episodic, notable in lifts/closed spaces and when he feels unwell; no exertional shortness of breath (can walk ~1 mile without SOB).\n  - Nausea intermittent, no vomiting; headaches at times.\n- Past medical history: hypothyroidism (previously on thyroxine) but stopped taking thyroxine since changing GP; no blood tests recently.\n- Medications/allergies: was taking thyroxine previously but currently not taking it; no allergies documented; no other medications recorded.\n- Family/social history: 35-year-old male, lawyer, married; recent job change and some stress; reduced physical activity recently; smoking/alcohol history not recorded.\n- Vital signs/exam findings: no vital signs or physical exam documented in the transcript.\n- Labs/imaging: none performed; clinician plans general bloods (FBC, renal/liver, thyroid tests, vitamin levels) and to arrange physical exam if bloods are unrevealing.",
